# Running coconut-app on a Physical iPhone

## Recommended daily workflow (works on corporate Wi‑Fi)

LAN Metro (`ios:dev:device`) does **not** work when device-to-device traffic is blocked. Use the **tunnel** script — this is the supported way to load the app on a physical iPhone:

```bash
cd ~/coconut-app

# First time or after native dependency changes — install dev build on phone:
npm run ios:dev:device:install

# Every dev session — Metro over ngrok (keep this terminal open):
npm run ios:dev:device:tunnel
```

Then on the phone: open **Coconut Dev**, scan the QR code from the terminal (or tap the dev server entry). You should see `iOS Bundled …` and app logs in the terminal.

**Do not use** `npm run ios:dev:device` alone on Databricks/corporate network — the phone cannot reach `192.168.x.x:8081`, so the app installs but never loads JS (no logs, blank/dev launcher).

### Script reference

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `ios:dev:device:install` | Build + install native app only (`--no-bundler`) |
| `ios:dev:device:tunnel` | **Start Metro with tunnel** — use this to run the app |
| `ios:dev:device` | Build + install + LAN Metro — home Wi‑Fi only |
| `ios:dev:device:start` | LAN Metro only (no rebuild) — home Wi‑Fi only |

Tunnel URL example from terminal: `https://….exp.direct` (also in the QR code).

### Tap to Pay on iPhone (error 2900)

If Pay shows **“Tap to Pay not in this build”** / Stripe `nativeErrorCode: 2900`, the installed app was signed **without** the proximity-reader entitlement. Metro reload cannot fix this — you need a **native rebuild**:

```bash
cd ~/coconut-app
npm run ios:dev:device:install
npm run ios:dev:device:tunnel
```

Also verify in [Apple Developer](https://developer.apple.com/account/) → Identifiers → **`com.coconut.app.dev`** → **Tap to Pay on iPhone** is enabled, and your **Development** provisioning profile includes that entitlement for your device.

### “No profiles for com.coconut.app.dev were found”

First install after switching bundle ID needs Xcode to **create** a Development profile. Run:

```bash
npm run ios:dev:device:install
```

`ios:dev:device:install` runs `xcodebuild` with `-allowProvisioningUpdates` (Expo alone skips this when `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` is already in the project). Approve any Xcode / Apple ID prompts for team **942BUGUD75**.

If it still fails:

1. Open `ios/Coconut.xcworkspace` in Xcode → **Signing & Capabilities** → enable **Automatically manage signing** for team **942BUGUD75**, then build once (⌘B).
2. Or create **Profiles → + → iOS App Development** for `com.coconut.app.dev`, include your iPhone, download, retry.

Optional: `export COCONUT_DEVICE_UDID=00008140-001A28601E83801C` if auto-detection picks the wrong device.

### After adding a native Expo module

If you see `Cannot find native module 'Expo…'` (e.g. after `expo install expo-image-manipulator`):

```bash
npm run ios:dev:device:install
npm run ios:dev:device:tunnel
```

Until then, receipt scan can still work if `coconut-app.dev` has the latest API (HEIC converted server-side).

## Environment constraints

- Corporate network (Databricks) blocks `registry.npmjs.org` and `repo1.maven.org` via `/etc/hosts`
- Use `--registry https://registry.npmmirror.com` for all `npm install` commands
- Hermes prebuilt binaries must be downloaded manually (see below)
- Device-to-device LAN is blocked — **always use `ios:dev:device:tunnel`**

## Device IDs

Update these if your phone UDID changes (`xcrun xctrace list devices`):

- **Expo / install script**: `00008140-001A28601E83801C` (Harshil’s iPhone) — or `export COCONUT_DEVICE_UDID=…` if detection fails
- **xcodebuild destination** (legacy doc): `id=00008150-000C5C8E3601401C`
- **Bundle ID (dev build)**: `com.coconut.app.dev` (see `app.config.js` with `APP_VARIANT=dev`)

## Step 1 — Fix app.config.js before every build

The `"react-native-reanimated"` expo plugin crashes the build on Node 20. Remove it before building (it's already applied to the native layer):

```js
// In app.config.js plugins array — remove this line:
"react-native-reanimated",
```

## Step 2 — Build the native app (optional manual xcodebuild)

Usually `npm run ios:dev:device:install` is enough. Manual build:

```bash
cd ~/coconut-app/ios
xcodebuild \
  -workspace Coconut.xcworkspace \
  -scheme Coconut \
  -configuration Debug \
  -destination 'id=YOUR_DEVICE_UDID' \
  DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=942BUGUD75 \
  -allowProvisioningUpdates \
  -allowProvisioningDeviceRegistration \
  build
```

If `pod install` is needed (new deps), Hermes tarballs must be pre-downloaded:

```bash
MAVEN_IP=$(nslookup repo1.maven.org 8.8.8.8 | grep Address | tail -1 | awk '{print $2}')
curl --resolve "repo1.maven.org:443:$MAVEN_IP" -L \
  "https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/facebook/react/react-native-artifacts/0.78.1/react-native-artifacts-0.78.1-hermes-framework-dSYM-debug.tar.gz" \
  -o /tmp/hermes-debug.tar.gz
HERMES_ENGINE_TARBALL_PATH=/tmp/hermes-debug.tar.gz pod install
```

## Trusting the dev certificate (once per install)

Settings → General → VPN & Device Management → your Apple ID → Trust

## Key files

- `.env` — `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://coconut-app.dev` and Clerk keys
- `ios/Podfile.properties.json` — `expo.jsEngine` must be `"hermes"`
